 \nL142:   * 【56†Sign up to our education newsletter†parliament.us16.list-manage.com】\nL143: \nL144: ## Shop\nL145: \nL146: Shop\nL147: \nL148: 【2†Close】 【2†Back】 【2†Close】\nL149: \nL150: ### In this section\nL151: \nL152:   * 【3†Shop home†www.shop.parliament.uk】\nL153: \nL154: 【57†UK Parliament】\nL155: # Parliament and Crown\nL156: \nL157: Along with the House of Commons and the House of Lords, the Crown is an integral part of the institution of Parliament. The King plays a constitutional role in opening and dissolving Parliament and approving Bills before they become law.\nL158: \nL159: 【58†Image: King's Speech】\nL160: \nL161: 【58†Image: Reflection of image】\nL162: \nL163: ### Parliament\nL164: \nL165: The highest legislative authority in the United Kingdom. Made up of the House of Commons, House of Lords and the King (who is the UK's current hereditary monarch).\nL166: ### Crown\nL167: \nL168: This is another way of referring to the monarchy - which is the oldest part of the system of government in this country. Time has reduced the power of the monarchy, and today it is broadly ceremonial. The current UK monarch is King Charles III.\nL169: \nL170: ### Appointing a government\nL171: \nL172: The day after a general election the King invites the leader of the party that won the most seats in the House of Commons to become Prime Minister and to form a government.\nL173: ### Opening and dissolving Parliament\nL174: \nL175: The Crown opens Parliament through the State Opening (marking the beginning of the Parliamentary year). The Crown also dissolves Parliament before a general election.\nL176: \nL177:   * 【59†More information on State Opening】\nL178: \nL179: ### King's Speech\nL180: \nL181: The Crown informs Parliament of the government's policy ideas and plans for new legislation in a speech delivered from the throne in the House of Lords. Although the King makes the speech the government draws up the content.\nL182: ### Royal Assent\nL183: \nL184: When a Bill has been approved by a majority in the House of Commons and the House of Lords it is formally agreed to by the Crown. This is known as the Royal Assent. This turns a Bill into an Act of Parliament, allowing it to become law in the UK.\nL185: \nL186: ## Glossary\nL187: \nL188: An alphabetical list of parliamentary terms with definitions.\nL189: \nL190: 【60†View glossary】\nL191: ###### Popular\nL192: \nL193:   * 【61†What's on in Parliament†whatson.parliament.uk】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMUNICIPALITY Definition & Meaning - Merriam-Webster (https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/municipality)\nciteturn10view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/municipality\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 202\nL0: 【0†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】 【1†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】\nL1: \nL2: [Input: Search Dictionary]\nL3: \nL4:   * 【2†Games】\nL5:   * 【3†Word of the Day】\nL6:   * 【4†Grammar】\nL7:   * 【5†Word Finder】\nL8:   * 【6†Slang】\nL9:   * 【7†Newsletters】\nL10:   * 【8†Wordplay】\nL11:   * 【9†Rhymes】\nL12:   * 【10†Thesaurus】\nL13:   * 【11†Join MWU†unabridged.merriam-webster.com】\nL14:   * More\nL15:     * 【2†Games】\nL16:     * 【3†Word of the Day】\nL17:     * 【4†Grammar】\nL18:     * 【8†Wordplay】\nL19:     * 【6†Slang】\nL20:     * 【9†Rhymes】\nL21:     * 【5†Word Finder】\nL22:     * 【7†Newsletters】\nL23:     * 【10†Thesaurus】\nL24:     * 【11†Join MWU†unabridged.merriam-webster.com】\nL25:     * Shop\nL26:     * 【12†Books†shop.merriam-webster.com】\nL27:     * 【13†Merch†merriamwebster.threadless.com】\nL28: \nL29: 【14†Dictionary】\nL30: \nL31:   * # municipality\nL32: ## 【15†noun】\nL33: \nL34: mu·​nic·​i·​pal·​i·​ty 【16†myu̇-ˌni-sə-ˈpa-lə-tē 】\nL35: \nL36: plural municipalities\nL37: \nL38: 【17†Synonyms of municipality】\nL39: \nL40: Simple Definition A Simple Definition is available from our Learner's Dictionary to help you understand the mea